From: Darius Mercadier <dmercadier@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 17:49:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [Backport] CVE-2026-79197: Use after free in V8 (3/4)

Cherry-pick of patch originally reviewed on
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8159283:
[debug] Deoptimize blackboxed OSR frames when stepping

When stepping out (Debug::PrepareStep) or stepping on throw
(Debug::PrepareStepOnThrow) across a blackboxed stack frame, V8 skips
FloodWithOneShot for that function. Consequently, the only mechanism
that deoptimizes frames during stack unwinding is the explicit
Deoptimizer::DeoptimizeFunction loop in PrepareStep and
PrepareStepOnThrow.

When DeoptimizeFunction is called without passing the frame's Code
object, it defaults to function->code(isolate), which points to the
function's default entrypoint code rather than any OSR machine code
attached to the stack frame. As a result, blackboxed OSR frames are
never deoptimized, and subsequent calls from their catch or return
blocks execute in optimized code without checking for step-in
breakpoints.

Pass frame->LookupCode() / js_frame->LookupCode() at both call sites
so blackboxed OSR frames are correctly deoptimized to bytecode when
stepping.

